# In-cluster deployment — TEMPLATE for the optional storage-class patch.
# Contract: .ai/spec/what/in-cluster-deployment.md rule 5 (the base PVC
# deliberately sets NO storageClassName: the cluster's default storage class
# applies — most portable. "Override by patch when the default is wrong.")
#
# Use this when your cluster has NO default storage class: the base PVC then
# never binds, and whoever made it work applied an explicit class server-side.
# Once the claim exists, spec.storageClassName is immutable — a live PVC
# carrying a class the manifest doesn't declare makes every `oc apply -k`
# error on it (harmlessly for the other objects, but noisily, and it breaks
# scripted applies). This patch makes the manifest match the bound claim.
#
# Procedure (mirrors the deploy-key wiring, rules 16a-16c):
# 1. Find your storage class:  oc get sc
#    (a class is the default iff its storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class
#    annotation is "true" — no default means the base PVC needs this patch)
# 2. Copy this file to pvc-patch.yaml (gitignored, like secret.yaml):
#       cp manifests/pvc-patch.yaml.example manifests/pvc-patch.yaml
# 3. Edit the value below to your cluster's class name.
# 4. Add the entry to your kustomization.yaml (the operator's local,
#    gitignored edit — not in the committed file):
#       patches:
#         - path: pvc-patch.yaml
# 5. Apply:  oc apply -k manifests/
#
# For a FIRST deployment on a no-default-class cluster this patch is also
# how you choose the class at creation time (the class must be set before
# the claim binds; after binding it is immutable).
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: ols-patroller-wiki
  namespace: ols-patroller
spec:
  storageClassName: lvms-vg1
